(6702386, 1002702, 20577, '<td valign="top">As a photographer I truly appreciate the idea of what apperas to be a class doing this challenge as a project. If this is the case then please do not be discouraged by the score... which I am sure is very low. You are allowed to enter an image up to 800 pixels wide and this is considerably smaller than that, so that is your first mistake and probably cut your score in half. This particular image is also hurt by the fact that it is sideways and nobody is "levitating", so I am guessing it may come in last place which is a sort of badge of honor on this site, so good luck with that!<br/> <br/>If photography is something that interests you then there is no better site to learn on than this one, so please kep submitting and learn as you go.</td>', 'As a photographer I truly appreciate the idea of what apperas to be a class doing this challenge as a project. If this is the case then please do not be discouraged by the score... which I am sure is very low. You are allowed to enter an image up to 800 pixels wide and this is considerably smaller than that, so that is your first mistake and probably cut your score in half. This particular image is also hurt by the fact that it is sideways and nobody is "levitating", so I am guessing it may come in last place which is a sort of badge of honor on this site, so good luck with that! If photography is something that interests you then there is no better site to learn on than this one, so please kep submitting and learn as you go.', '2012-03-07 02:48:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6702388, 1002703, 20577, '<td valign="top">As a photographer I truly appreciate the idea of what appears to be a class doing this challenge as a project. If this is the case then please do not be discouraged by the score... which I am sure is very low. You are allowed to enter an image up to 800 pixels wide and this is considerably smaller than that, so that is your first mistake and probably cut your score in half. A faster shutter speed would have helped freeze the subject giving the appearance of levitation. Additionally, Natsumi generally takes photographs that seem to be more natural even though they are staged. This one seems staged and is more of an action shot then a levitation shot.<br/> <br/>If photography is something that interests you then there is no better site to learn on than this one, so please kep submitting and learn as you go.</td>', 'As a photographer I truly appreciate the idea of what appears to be a class doing this challenge as a project. If this is the case then please do not be discouraged by the score... which I am sure is very low. You are allowed to enter an image up to 800 pixels wide and this is considerably smaller than that, so that is your first mistake and probably cut your score in half. A faster shutter speed would have helped freeze the subject giving the appearance of levitation. Additionally, Natsumi generally takes photographs that seem to be more natural even though they are staged. This one seems staged and is more of an action shot then a levitation shot. If photography is something that interests you then there is no better site to learn on than this one, so please kep submitting and learn as you go.', '2012-03-07 02:48:32.000000', NULL, 1),
